From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: samsung-dsim: start J701F inherited PLL from off

The bounded native-dsimdiag2-01 trial finds PLL_EN and LINK_STATUS lock set
before the first PLL programming, but no fresh completion. Error cleanup
turns off the PLL; the following initialization completes immediately.
Vendor code also explicitly handles an already-stable bootloader PLL.

For the existing privileged J701F trial only, stop inherited DSIM clocks
before reset when PLL_EN is set. This uses the same cleanup routine as the
successful retry; leave PLL search, IRQ masks and every other device
intact.
Do not reset the shared DISPAUD power domain. Host regression checks real
init ordering and failure cleanup; hardware verification is pending.
---

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
@@ -1693,6 +1693,11 @@
 	if (dsi->state & DSIM_STATE_INITIALIZED)
 		return 0;
 
+	/* An inherited enabled PLL need not produce a new PLL_STABLE event. */
+	if (samsung_dsim_j701f_trial(dsi) &&
+	    (samsung_dsim_read(dsi, DSIM_PLLCTRL_REG) & DSIM_PLL_EN))
+		samsung_dsim_disable_clock(dsi);
+
 	samsung_dsim_reset(dsi);
 	samsung_dsim_enable_irq(dsi);
 
